# e16_interval.gbnf: the four sleep intervals of rules_e16.c, letter for letter, and
# one bounded sentence of reason. The literals are I60, I300, I900 and I3600, for 60,
# 300, 900 and 3600 seconds, in the order of the rule's name table, so I60 comes first
# and is what the stub answers in CI. The "decision" key keeps the house name so that
# tools/agreement.py reads it unchanged. The reason is 10 to 160 characters of letters,
# digits, space, comma, full stop and percent, ending in a full stop, so the
# end-of-generation token is reachable only after a complete sentence; the class admits
# no quote, no brace and no newline, so the object always closes and the log's CSV
# quoting stays simple. The stub expands every character class to nothing, so in CI the
# answer is {"decision":"I60","reason":"."}, which the oracle file expects on every row.
# ws admits spaces and tabs only, never a newline.
root ::= "{" ws "\"decision\"" ws ":" ws decision ws "," ws "\"reason\"" ws ":" ws reason ws "}"
decision ::= "\"I60\"" | "\"I300\"" | "\"I900\"" | "\"I3600\""
reason ::= "\"" [A-Za-z0-9 ,.%]{9,159} "." "\""
ws ::= [ \t]*
